  <data name="Controls_Settings_AboutSettingsSection__Auto_600.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Wavee is a third-party Spotify client. To make Recently Played, play counts, and recommendations work, the app sends the same minimum set of playback events to Spotify that the official client sends (the &amp;quot;gabo&amp;quot; telemetry pipeline): track URI, context URI, ms played, reason started/ended, audio format. Nothing else. No third-party analytics, no Wavee-operated server, no remote crash reporting. Your Spotify credentials are encrypted on disk via Windows DPAPI; the encryption is bound to your Windows user account. AI features (lyrics meaning, song themes) run entirely on-device via Phi Silica on Copilot+ PCs and never leave the machine.</value>
  </data>
